  "output": "I'll analyze the provided codebase files for each performance concern.\n\n## Performance Analysis: VoidRift\n\n---\n\n### 1. N+1 I/O Patterns\n\n**`src/codemap/index.ts` — synchronous file reads in walk loop**\n\nEvery call to `generateCodeMap` reads N files synchronously in a loop. On a large workspace this serializes hundreds of disk reads.\n\n```typescript\n// Current — O(N) synchronous reads, one per file\nfunction walk(dir: string, root: string, depth: number): CodeMapEntry[] {\n  for (const item of items.sort()) {\n    if (CODE_EXTENSIONS.has(ext)) {\n      symbols = extractSymbols(fullPath);  // readFileSync here\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFix: batch with `Promise.all` using async fs, or at minimum defer symbol extraction until actually needed:\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFile } from \"fs/promises\";\n\nasync function extractSymbolsAsync(filePath: string): Promise<string[]> {\n  const content = await readFile(filePath, \"utf-8\");\n  // ... same regex logic\n}\n\n// In walk, collect paths then batch:\nconst symbolJobs = codeFiles.map(p => extractSymbolsAsync(p));\nconst allSymbols = await Promise.all(symbolJobs);\n```\n\n**`src/bootstrap/validate.ts` — `readFileSync` via dynamic `require` in skill loop**\n\n```typescript\n// Current — dynamic require + readFileSync inside loop\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  const raw = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n```\n\nFix: import `readFileSync` at the top, and batch reads:\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\";\n\n// read all at once outside the loop if possible, or at least avoid dynamic require\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  const raw = readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Re-renders\n\nNo React components are present in the provided files. The UI layer (`main.tsx`, Ink components) isn't included — this section would need those files to audit.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n**`src/adapters/factory.ts` / `src/codemap/summarizer.ts` — new LangChain client on every call**\n\n`createTierAdapter` is called on every summarization and MCP sampling, creating a new `ChatOpenAI`/`ChatAnthropic` instance (with connection pools, auth, retry state) each time:\n\n```typescript\n// src/codemap/summarizer.ts — current\nconst resolved = createTierAdapter(\"flash\", config);  // new client every invocation\nresolved.client.cache = getModelCache();\n```\n\nFix: add a module-level adapter cache in `factory.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n// src/adapters/factory.ts\nconst _adapterCache = new Map<string, ResolvedModel>();\n\nexport function createAdapter(modelName: string, appConfig: VoidRiftConfig): ResolvedModel {\n  const cacheKey = `${modelName}:${appConfig.maxConcurrentAgents}`;\n  if (_adapterCache.has(cacheKey)) return _adapterCache.get(cacheKey)!;\n  const config = appConfig.models[modelName];\n  if (!config) throw new Error(`Model \"${modelName}\" not found in config`);\n  const resolved = { name: modelName, config, client: createClient(config, appConfig.maxConcurrentAgents) };\n  _adapterCache.set(cacheKey, resolved);\n  return resolved;\n}\n```\n\n**`src/codemap/cache.ts` — `IndexCache` not wired into `summarizeFileWithFlash`**\n\n`IndexCache` stores file summaries by content hash but `summarizeFileWithFlash` never consults it — it hits the model every time for the same unchanged file:\n\n```typescript\n// src/codemap/summarizer.ts — fix: use IndexCache\nexport async function summarizeFileWithFlash(\n  path: string,\n  content: string,\n  config: VoidRiftConfig,\n  cache?: IndexCache   // inject the cache\n): Promise<{ summary: string; totalLines: number }> {\n  const lines = content.split(\"\\n\");\n  const totalLines = lines.length;\n\n  if (totalLines <= (config.summarizeThreshold ?? 500)) {\n    return { summary: content, totalLines };\n  }\n\n  if (cache) {\n    const hash = cache.computeHash(content);\n    const hit = cache.get(path, hash);\n    if (hit) return { summary: hit.summary, totalLines: hit.totalLines };\n  }\n\n  // ... model call ...\n\n  if (cache && summary.length > 0) {\n    const hash = cache.computeHash(content);\n    cache.set(path, hash, summary, totalLines);\n  }\n  return { summary, totalLines };\n}\n```\n\n**`src/codemap/cache.ts` — disk write on every `set`**\n\nEvery individual cache entry write flushes the entire JSON file to disk:\n\n```typescript\n// Current — write on every set\npublic set(...): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { ... };\n  this.save();  // disk write here\n}\n```\n\nFix: debounce the save:\n\n```typescript\nprivate _saveTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;\n\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  if (!this._saveTimer) {\n    this._saveTimer = setTimeout(() => {\n      this._saveTimer = null;\n      this.save();\n    }, 500);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**`src/events/bus.ts` — closure accumulation on repeated subscribe**\n\n`subscribe` allocates a new `wrapped` closure on each call. If callers never invoke the returned unsubscribe function (e.g., fire-and-forget event handlers), listeners accumulate for the lifetime of the process:\n\n```typescript\n// The wrapped closure keeps `listener` alive indefinitely if unsub() isn't called\nconst wrapped = async (event: any) => { ... };\nthis.emitter.on(type, wrapped);\nreturn () => this.emitter.off(type, wrapped);\n```\n\nThe `maxListeners` ceiling of 100 will warn but not prevent this. Enforce unsubscription at call sites and add a leak detector:\n\n```typescript\n// Option: warn if a high-churn event type accumulates many listeners\nsubscribe(type: string, listener: (event: any) => void): () => void {\n  if (this.emitter.listenerCount(type) > 20) {\n    console.warn(`[EventBus] ${type} has ${this.emitter.listenerCount(type)} listeners — possible leak`);\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**`src/bootstrap/cli.ts` — elicitation handler creates a new 120s subscription on every elicitation**\n\n```typescript\nmcp.setElicitationHandler(async (message: string) => {\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const unsub = container.bus.subscribe(\"TOOL_CONFIRMATION_RESPONSE\", (event: any) => {\n      // ...\n    });\n    setTimeout(() => { unsub(); resolve({ action: \"deny\" }); }, 120_000);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nIf elicitations arrive faster than 120s apart, multiple response listeners stack. Use a `Map` keyed by `requestId` instead:\n\n```typescript\nconst pendingElicitations = new Map<string, (approved: boolean) => void>();\n\nconst unsub = container.bus.subscribe(\"TOOL_CONFIRMATION_RESPONSE\", (event: any) => {\n  const { requestId, approved } = event.payload;\n  const resolve = pendingElicitations.get(requestId);\n  if (resolve) {\n    pendingElicitations.delete(requestId);\n    resolve(approved);\n  }\n});\n\nmcp.setElicitationHandler(async (message: string) => {\n  const requestId = `elicit-${Date.now()}`;\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      pendingElicitations.delete(requestId);\n      resolve({ action: \"deny\" });\n    }, 120_000);\n\n    pendingElicitations.set(requestId, (approved) => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      resolve(approved ? { action: \"accept\" } : { action: \"deny\" });\n    });\n\n    container.bus.publish(\"TOOL_CONFIRMATION_REQUEST\", { ... });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`src/logging/audit.ts` — `attach()` not guarded against double-call**\n\nIf `attach()` is called twice (e.g., session restart without full teardown), all event listeners double up. Add a guard:\n\n```typescript\nprivate _attached = false;\n\nattach(bus: EventBus): () => void {\n  if (this._attached) throw new Error(\"AuditLogger already attached\");\n  this._attached = true;\n  const unsubs: Array<() => void> = [];\n  // ...\n  return () => {\n    this._attached = false;\n    unsubs.forEach(u => u());\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**`src/bootstrap/validate.ts` — `Array.includes` on every agent ID check is O(n²)**\n\n```typescript\n// Current — allAgentIds is an array, .includes() is O(n) per call\nconst allAgentIds = [\n  ...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id),\n  ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id),\n];\n\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  const invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !allAgentIds.includes(id));  // O(n) each\n```\n\nFix: one-line change, O(1) lookups:\n\n```typescript\nconst allAgentIds = new Set([\n  ...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id),\n  ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id),\n]);\n\nconst invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !allAgentIds.has(id));\n```\n\n**`src/codemap/index.ts` — triple regex match per line in `extractSymbols`**\n\nEach line in every file runs up to 3 separate regex evaluations even when the first two would have matched:\n\n```typescript\nfor (const line of lines) {\n  const trimmed = line.trim();\n  const exportMatch = trimmed.match(/^export\\s+.../);   // regex 1\n  if (exportMatch) { ... continue; }\n  if (trimmed.match(/^export\\s+default\\s+\\w/)) { ... continue; }  // regex 2 — subset of regex 1\n  if (line[0] && line[0] !== \" \" && line[0] !== \"\\t\") {\n    const topLevel = trimmed.match(/^(?:async\\s+)?.../)  // regex 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `export default` check is redundant — a single broader export regex can capture both, and the character check can short-circuit earlier:\n\n```typescript\nconst EXPORT_RE = /^export\\s+(?:default\\s+)?(?:async\\s+)?(function|class|interface|type|const|let|enum)\\s+(\\w+)/;\nconst TOPLEVEL_RE = /^(?:async\\s+)?(function|class|interface|type|enum)\\s+(\\w+)/;\n\nfor (const line of lines) {\n  if (!line[0] || line[0] === \" \" || line[0] === \"\\t\") continue;  // fast skip\n  const trimmed = line.trim();\n  const m = trimmed.match(EXPORT_RE) ?? trimmed.match(TOPLEVEL_RE);\n  if (m) symbols.push(`${m[1]} ${m[2]}`);\n  else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"export default \")) symbols.push(\"default export\");\n}\n```\n\nMove the regex literals outside the function so they're compiled once, not on every `extractSymbols` call.\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Issue | Impact | Effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| `createTierAdapter` not cached | High — model client created per LLM call | Low |\n| `IndexCache` not wired to `summarizeFileWithFlash` | High — redundant model calls on unchanged files | Low |\n| `elicitationHandler` subscription stacking | Medium — leaks listeners under load | Low |\n| `IndexCache.set` writes disk every entry | Medium — spikes during indexing | Low |\n| `allAgentIds.includes` O(n²) | Low — only at startup | Trivial |\n| Regex compiled inside loop | Low — codemap is startup-only | Low |\n| Walk using sync I/O in loop | Medium — slow on large repos | Medium |\n",
